# Family A34: the Pub/Sub client generation (drivers/gcppubsub =
# cloud.google.com/go/pubsub/v2 against drivers/gcppubsub/v1compat = the
# deprecated v1 API). See hack/bakeoff.sh.
#
# the benchmark configuration row A34's arms are two CLIENT LIBRARIES in two modules,
# which is the one shape `hack/bakeoff.sh` could not express: it runs one
# `go test` in one package, and §9.4 step 2 wants the arms interleaved inside
# one invocation. The two can only be in one package if that package imports
# both, and the only one in this repository that does is the v1compat driver's
# own test binary -- it already imports drivers/gcppubsub for the shared
# semantics, for the cross-generation equivalence suite and for the capability
# table both arms answer.
#
# Measuring both arms in one binary is also what makes the comparison honest in
# the way that matters most: one process, one pstest service instance, one gRPC
# connection, one Go runtime and one GOMAXPROCS for both arms. Two runs in two
# processes would differ by whatever else the host did between them.
MODDIR=drivers/gcppubsub/v1compat
PKG=.
BENCH=BenchmarkPubSubClient
REF=v2
AUTO_KEY=pubsub_client
KINDS_TEST=TestPubSubClientKindsList
# Nothing binds to this family's winner: which Pub/Sub client generation is
# canonical is ADR-013's decision and not an `Auto` constant, exactly as family
# A11's Kafka client library is not one. §9.1 row A34's tentative default is
# "v2 default", which is a statement about the driver's TIER (§7.1) and about
# the driver page rather than about a generated binding -- and v1compat is
# shipped as an experimental migration path whatever the numbers say, because
# the upstream module is deprecated and will stop building.
AUTO_FILE=-
ADR=13
TITLE="Pub/Sub client generation: pubsub/v2 against the v1 compatibility adapter (A34)"

#
# CRITERION is the benchmark configuration's decision column for this row, quoted.
# MATRIX is the IQMQ_BENCH_MATRIX grid the campaign measures the family at.
# DECIDED_AT names the benchmark-name segments the criterion is read at, and
# DECIDED_ON the metrics; `make bench-lint` lists the family's benchmarks at
# the declared grid and fails when a term or a metric is missing from the rows
# every kind has in common, which is the only data `bakeoff decide` reads.
CRITERION="correctness, maintenance, native comparison -> v2 default"
# MATRIX=default is the only grid: the benchmark states its own sweep inside
# its name -- four operations at three payload sizes -- and has no
# IQMQ_BENCH_MATRIX branch, so there is no wider grid to ask for.
MATRIX=default
DECIDED_AT="publish batch consume endtoend 64B 1KiB 64KiB"
DECIDED_ON="ns/op allocs/op B/op msgs/s"
# What this family's measurement cannot produce, and where the evidence for it
# lives instead. §9.1 row A34 names three things and TWO of them are not
# benchmark metrics at all.
#
# NB: entries are separated by ";" and nothing inside an entry may contain one,
# or the parser reads the fragment after it as a key with no text -- which is
# what `make bench-lint` refuses on a first draft of such a file.
CRITERION_GAP="correctness=a correctness GATE rather than a metric, and the arms share every line of the driver above drivers/gcppubsub/internal/psapi, so what can differ is the client library. It is established by TestModel in drivers/gcppubsub/v1compat (at-least-once, an acknowledgement being terminal, a nack redelivering, order within an ordering key, and §4.3's answer to a second settlement, each run through both arms), by TestBothArmsAnswerOneCapabilityTable, and by TestTheArmsAreWireCompatible, which publishes through each generation and consumes through the other; maintenance=a fact about the UPSTREAM module and not something any measurement can report. cloud.google.com/go/pubsub is marked deprecated by its own module (go get prints \"module cloud.google.com/go/pubsub is deprecated: use cloud.google.com/go/pubsub/v2 instead\"), which is the whole of the evidence and is why v2 is the default whatever the numbers say; native-comparison=the raw-client baseline is benchmarks/native-baselines/pubsub, which measures cloud.google.com/go/pubsub/v2 against the pinned emulator CONTAINER. It is not comparable row for row with this family, which measures both arms against the in-process pstest service: a driver number and a baseline number are only comparable when the service is the same, and the container is what the baseline uses (the performance budgets layer 3); p99-and-container-latency=the service here is the in-process pstest fake and not the pinned emulator container, which is deliberate for the ns/op half -- a container's service cost is common-mode and both arms pay it identically -- and is a real gap for any latency figure, where a container's gRPC stack is part of what a caller waits for. conformance/suites/gcppubsub_test.go is what runs against the container"
